  "name": null,
  "problem": "The temperature of a metal rod, measured in degrees Celsius, is given by the function $T(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the heating began. The values of $T(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T(t)$ | $18$ | $21$ | $27$ | $30$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the temperature when $t=12$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=12$ is\n{{field-1}} degrees Celsius per hour.",
